    "computation_explanation": "incomplete_count is computed as the number of unacknowledged TCP handshakes in incomplete_window whose timeout (2.0s) has expired within the preceding 1.0-second sliding evaluation window. Under a table size of 20,000 at 20,000 pps, entries live only ~1.0 second (20,000 / 20,000 pps) before being capacity-evicted in FIFO order. Because capacity-evicted entries do NOT count as incomplete handshakes (to protect benign flash crowds from false alarms), zero entries reach the 2.0s completion timeout, resulting in 0 expired handshakes and 0 alerts under the 20k cap. With a 160,000 table size, entries live up to 8.0 seconds at 20k pps (and 2.0 seconds at 80k pps), allowing entries to reach the 2.0s timeout and fire Condition A (incomplete_count >= 15 with distinct sources >= 3)."
